      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BLINDATO (4) is the one to beat after resuming with a sound sixth in a BM62 over 1600m at Ballarat, beaten just under three lengths after jumping awkwardly. He rises to BM66 level, but gets useful weight relief, has already placed at this track and brings a profile with upside second-up. DEFICIT (8) drops from Saturday company after being well held at Morphettville Parks, but the return toward 1800m helps given he has two wins at the distance and his prior fourth at Morphettville was sound enough for this. FOX GEM (2) resumed with a solid seventh in a BM70 at Strathalbyn, beaten just over two lengths from well back, and while the rise from 1350m asks for improvement, his one win and five placings from nine starts at around 1800m keep him in the mix. VAN ROY (1) finished seventh last start when resuming at Donald over 1620m. Fitter second up and should give this a shake.",
